WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.939 --> 00:00:10.799
As an inquisitive and interpretative species,
we are always working to examine, critique,

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:14.559
and improve the world around us.

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:18.810
We want what’s best for the world and we
all like to believe that we know what’s

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.860
best for it.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:27.430
As a result, we constantly judge and critique
the things we encounter in life, including

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.810
other people.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:37.679
This innate competitive self-confidence is
well-intended, but it often results in a pessimistic

00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:40.739
judgment of other people.

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:46.129
What we must understand is that there are
two sides to the coin of self-confidence.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:54.820
On one side, it is good to have a unique perspective
of the world that we believe in and work for.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:01.719
But on the other side, we must not take it
so far as to let it become negative and limiting.

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:09.610
Progression, revelation, and wonder cultivate
outside of our bubbles of ideology, and if

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:17.580
our self-righteousness is too rigid, we close
our self off from such opportunity.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:23.830
We must balance both sides and free ourselves
of rigid self-righteousness.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:31.180
We must remind ourselves that just as valuable
as our views and ideals are to us, so are

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.920
other views and ideals to other people.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:41.880
If we do not want others to discard and belittle
the ways in which we live, we must ensure

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:47.930
that we are not discarding or belittling the
way in which others live.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:54.840
We must work to develop and improve our sense
of the world through open-mindedness.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:00.220
We must utilize our unique human capacity
for empathy.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:06.520
When you focus on empathy, you understand
that just as others are imperfect, so are

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.800
you.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:15.060
When you admit this, you balance judgment
out and neutralize its harmful effects.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:20.610
You no longer feel as though you are above
anyone, and as a result, no longer feel as

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.910
though you are beneath anyone.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:31.490
In reducing your degree of self-righteousness,
you reduce irrational and unnecessary negativity

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:33.530
in your life.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:41.250
In its place forms a heightened openness and
opportunity to learn, experience, and connect.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:46.900
You become open to life, and life becomes
open

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.600
to you.

